---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/Sections/PageHeader.astro";

const POLICY_EFFECTIVE_DATE = "To be set at publication";
const SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | BEMA - Healthcare Access for Florida's Working Families"
  description="Learn how BEMA Health Incorporated collects, uses, and shares information when you visit this website or contact our team."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="This policy explains how information is handled when you visit this website or contact BEMA Health Incorporated."
  />

  <section class="section-pad bg-bema-white">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-4xl prose-headings:text-bema-green prose-p:text-bema-green/85 prose-li:text-bema-green/85 prose-a:text-bema-green">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {POLICY_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>BEMA Health Incorporated is a Florida nonprofit corporation that coordinates access to care. BEMA Health Incorporated is not a medical provider.</p>
        <p>This policy applies to this website and explains how information is handled when you visit the site or submit a form.</p>

        <h2>Information you give us</h2>
        <p>You may give us information through the Contact form or either version of the Get Started form.</p>

        <h3>Contact form</h3>
        <p>The Contact form includes your name, email address, optional phone number, subject, and message.</p>

        <h3>Get Started form for individuals</h3>
        <p>The individual form includes a form type value, name, email address, optional phone number, optional ZIP Code, who the request is for, the total number of people when applicable, preferred method of contact, and an optional message.</p>

        <h3>Get Started form for employers</h3>
        <p>The employer form includes a form type value, contact name, business name, email address, optional phone number, number of employees, work arrangement, preferred method of contact, and an optional message.</p>

        <p>Form submissions are delivered by email to a BEMA Google Workspace mailbox. Submissions are processed by our hosting provider, Vercel, on their way to email. This website does not keep a database of form submissions. We use the information to respond to your inquiry and follow up with you.</p>
        <p><strong>Please do not include personal health information in any form on this site.</strong> Do not include medical or health details, diagnoses, or payment or account numbers in any form submission.</p>

        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
        <p>When you visit the site, Google Analytics collects information such as page views, interactions, approximate location, and device and browser details using cookie identifiers.</p>
        {SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION && <p>Microsoft Clarity collects information about how visitors interact with pages.</p>}
        <p>To display our fonts, your browser requests font resources from Google. Google receives standard request information such as your IP address and browser details.</p>
        <p>Our hosting and network providers also process standard technical information needed to deliver and protect the site. This may include your IP address, browser and device details, pages requested, and timestamps.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies to provide the functions described in this policy.</p>
        {SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION && <p>Microsoft Clarity also uses cookies and similar technologies for the purposes described below.</p>}
        {/* CONFIRM: match against cookies observed in production DevTools */}
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Provider</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Type</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>_ga</code></td>
                <td>Google Analytics</td>
                <td>Distinguishes visitors for site traffic measurement.</td>
                <td>First party</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>{"_ga_<container ID>"}</code></td>
                <td>Google Analytics</td>
                <td>Maintains information used to measure site activity.</td>
                <td>First party</td>
              </tr>
              {SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION && (
                <>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>_clck</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Stores a Clarity visitor identifier and preferences for this site.</td>
                    <td>First party</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>_clsk</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Connects multiple page views by a visitor into a single Clarity session recording.</td>
                    <td>First party</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>CLID</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Identifies the first time Clarity saw this visitor on any site using Clarity.</td>
                    <td>Third party</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>ANONCHK</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Indicates whether a Microsoft browser identifier is transferred to an advertising cookie. Clarity does not use that cookie, so the value is always 0.</td>
                    <td>Third party</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>MR</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Indicates whether to refresh the Microsoft browser identifier.</td>
                    <td>Third party</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>MUID</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Identifies unique web browsers visiting Microsoft sites. Microsoft uses it for advertising, site analytics, and other operational purposes.</td>
                    <td>Third party</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>SM</code></td>
                    <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
                    <td>Synchronizes the Microsoft browser identifier across Microsoft domains.</td>
                    <td>Third party</td>
                  </tr>
                </>
              )}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>You can use your browser controls to block or delete cookies.</p>
        {SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION && <p>Microsoft states that Clarity sets no cookies when browser cookies are disabled.</p>}
        <p>You may also use the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt out add on</a>.</p>
        {/* CONFIRM: verify that the Google Analytics opt out link resolves */}

        <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>We use Google Analytics to understand traffic to this site only. It collects page views, interactions, approximate location, and device and browser details using cookie identifiers.</p>
        <p>Google states that Google Analytics does not log or store individual IP addresses. Event level data is kept for a limited period set in our Google Analytics account.</p>
        <p>We do not enable Google Analytics advertising features.</p>
        {/* CONFIRM: Google signals and advertising features off in GA4 admin */}
        <p>Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a> and in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p>

        {SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION && (
          <section>
            <h2>Microsoft Clarity</h2>
            <p>Microsoft Clarity records how visitors interact with pages, including clicks, scrolls, mouse movement, and page rendering. It presents this information through session replays and heatmaps to help us improve site usability.</p>
            <p>We use strict masking so page text is masked in recordings.</p>
            {/* CONFIRM: strict masking is enabled in the Clarity project settings */}
            <p>Microsoft acts as an independent controller of Clarity data under its terms and not on our behalf. Clarity data is stored in Microsoft Azure.</p>
            <p>Learn more in <a href="https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=521839">Microsoft's privacy statement</a>.</p>
            {/* CONFIRM: legal review of Clarity Terms of Use healthcare content clause before publishing this section */}
          </section>
        )}

        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to respond to inquiries, follow up with people who contact us, understand and improve the site, maintain security, and comply with legal obligations.</p>

        <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
        <p>We share information with service providers that help us operate the site and communicate with visitors. These providers include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Workspace for email</li>
          <li>Google Analytics for site traffic measurement</li>
          <li>Google Fonts for font delivery</li>
          {SHOW_CLARITY_SECTION && <li>Microsoft Clarity for site interaction measurement</li>}
          <li>Vercel for hosting</li>
          <li>Cloudflare for DNS and network services</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Each provider receives information relevant to the service it provides.</p>
        <p>We may also disclose information where required by law. We do not sell personal information.</p>
        {/* CONFIRM: legal review of this statement */}

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>We keep form messages only as long as needed to respond and maintain appropriate organizational records.</p>
        {/* CONFIRM: founders decide form email retention period; hardening item */}

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>We use reasonable safeguards intended to protect information. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure.</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This site is not directed to children under 18.</p>
        {/* CONFIRM: founders and counsel review wording; BEMA serves families and Get Started asks who the request is for, including Child */}

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>This site may link to websites operated by other organizations. This policy does not cover those websites. Review their privacy information before providing information to them.</p>

        <h2>Your choices and contact</h2>
        <p>You can use the cookie controls described above. For questions or requests about your information, contact <a href="mailto:support@bemahealth.org">support@bemahealth.org</a>.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy as our practices or legal obligations change. Updates will be posted on this page with a new Last updated date.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
